# Reactor failure behaviour for every Maven invocation in this repository.
#
# --fail-at-end keeps the reactor going after a module fails, so a single red
# module can no longer hide the integration tests of the modules that follow it.
# Without it, `mvn verify` halted at the first failing module and left the *IT
# classes of every later module unexecuted, which reported a much smaller
# failure surface than the build actually had. The build still FAILS: the
# failure is reported at the end, together with every other module's outcome,
# and modules that depend on a failed module are still skipped.
#
# Rationale: docs/decision-log.md, section 53.
--fail-at-end
